           android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE / _DATA_SYNC
         plus <uses-feature> for camera, camera.autofocus, usb.host, bluetooth.
    -->
    <!-- Kati asks for exactly what it uses. Every permission here is a line on
         the Play data-safety form and a reason for a user to distrust the app,
         so the stock template's camera, microphone, location, media-library,
         Bluetooth and USB requests are deliberately absent: Kati is a local
         tracker that talks to a handful of JSON APIs. Calendar permissions
         arrive with the CalendarContract work, not before. -->

    <!-- Third-party metadata APIs (TMDB, TVmaze, AniList) -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <!-- DELETED by K-01 permission-trim: ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE, which mob_new
         0.4.33 added for `Mob.Device.network_state/0` and the `:network`
         events. Nothing in Kati reads either — `Kati.Media.Tmdb` reports a
         failed fetch from the failure itself ("Could not reach TMDB. Hand-typed
         titles still work.") rather than by asking the OS first. A permission
         with no caller is one the Play data-safety form cannot answer for,
         which is what `Kati.HostHardeningTest` asserts.

         MainActivity's generated `registerDefaultNetworkCallback` is wrapped in
         a bare `catch (_: Throwable)`, so without the permission it takes the
         SecurityException and publishes nothing — which is the same as now. -->

    <!-- Release and air-date reminders -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM"
        android:minSdkVersion="31" />
    <!-- Backed by KatiBootReceiver below. AlarmManager drops every pending
         alarm on reboot, so without the receiver this permission was requested
         and never used, and reminders vanished silently after a restart. -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED" />

    <!-- KATI-BEGIN(K-26 read-calendar) mob_new=0.4.20
         Read-only. Kati mirrors the device's calendars; write-back is a
